  "body_html": "<h1>Dominant Strategy Profile is a Nash Equilibrium</h1>\n<p>If every player $i$ plays a weakly dominant strategy $s_i$, then the resulting\nprofile $\\sigma = (s_i)_{i \\in I}$ is a Nash equilibrium.</p>",
  "proof_html": "<p>A weakly dominant strategy weakly dominates every alternative. In particular,\nfor any player $i$ and any deviation $s'_i$, we have\n$u_i(\\sigma[i \\mapsto s'_i]) \\le u_i(\\sigma)$. This means each player is best\nresponding, so $\\sigma$ is a Nash equilibrium. $\\square$</p>",
